00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.500
LILIANA YU: What do the
gaming, retail, education,

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:10.160
and agricultural
industries have in common?

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:12.590
Many of them are
optimizing their workflows

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:17.180
and increasing their efficiency
using Google Compute Engine.

00:00:17.180 --> 00:00:20.270
Google Compute Engine lets you
create and run virtual machines

00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:22.070
on Google infrastructure.

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:25.580
Compute Engine offers scale,
performance, and value

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.670
that allows you to easily
launch large compute clusters

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:30.860
on Google's infrastructure.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.590
You can run your Windows
applications on Google Compute

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:36.320
Engine and take advantage
of many benefits

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.600
available to virtual
machine instances,

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:40.850
such as reliable
storage options,

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.470
the speed of the Google
network, and auto scaling.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:47.360
In this Qwik Start
Lab, you will learn

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.270
how to launch a Windows Server
instance in Google Compute

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:55.190
Engine and connect it to using
the remote desktop protocol.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:59.390
You do not need a Google Cloud
Platform account or project.

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:02.390
An account, project,
and associated resources

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.170
are provided to you as part
of this lab on Qwiklabs.

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:09.500
This is the second lab in
the GCP Essentials Quest.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.490
A quest is a series of related
labs that form a learning path.

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.770
Completing this quest
earns you this badge

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:17.630
to recognize your achievement.

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:20.390
You can make your
badge or badges public

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.060
and link to them in your online
resume or social media account.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.940
Next up on your quest
is Getting Started

00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:28.150
with Google Shell and GCloud.

